    a: >-
      Pressurised ships carry LPG at ambient temperature in pressure tanks and
      suit small parcels. Semi-refrigerated ships combine pressure and cooling and
      can work with both pressurised and refrigerated terminals. Fully
      refrigerated ships carry the cargo at atmospheric pressure, at about −50 °C.
